# Local development caches and script artifacts. `.gitignore` already keeps these
# out of the repository, but a `.vercelignore` REPLACES `.gitignore` for uploads made
# by the Vercel CLI — so without this block a `vercel deploy` from a workstation
# uploads whatever the local scripts left on disk. In #179 that was 2.9 GB of SRTM
# tiles under data/srtm-cache/, which then landed inside nine Functions.
data/
db-clone/
.dedupe-out/
.demote-out/
.merge-out/

# Other development files
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local 